# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CODEOWNERS — ownership for review routing
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Format: <pattern>  <@user-or-team>...
# Last matching rule wins (so put broader patterns first, narrower
# patterns later). Patterns are gitignore-style.
#
# When a PR touches a path listed here, GitHub will request review
# from the matching owner. Combined with branch protection (require
# review from CODEOWNERS), this guarantees that a PR touching these
# paths can't merge without the listed reviewer's approval.
#
# External pull requests are not currently reviewed (see
# CONTRIBUTING.md), so these rules exist for maintainer PRs —
# they are a guardrail on the paths below, not a triage queue. The
# rules stay silent until `@withso/zeros-maintainers` exists as a team
# with read access to this repo, and until "Require review from Code
# Owners" is enabled in Settings → Branches.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Catch-all (so unconfigured paths still notify someone)
*                                       @withso/zeros-maintainers

